{"duration_api_ms":155014,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"eb070e55-22c4-41e6-a24a-be0d3245bba1","total_cost_usd":0.5490257999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":60,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38753,"cache_read_input_tokens":1293624,"output_tokens":13103,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1940},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38753,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2476,"cache_read_input_tokens":53136,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2641,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2641},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4024,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0041389999999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":60,"outputTokens":13103,"cacheReadInputTokens":1293624,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38753,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5448867999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1940,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":31,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Built and deployed a small SQLite-backed CGI \\\"inventory application\\\" (add/list items) served by httpd on node1's TCP port 8181, with SELinux/mandatory access control kept in enforcing mode throughout. Configured semanage port to label 8181 as http_port_t (so the confined httpd_t domain is permitted to bind it), set correct file contexts (httpd_sys_script_exec_t for the CGI script, httpd_sys_rw_content_t for the writable data directory), opened the port in firewalld, verified end-to-end functionality (GET renders inventory table, POST adds an item and persists it), then executed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id and healthy baseline, issued systemctl reboot with the ack returned before disconnect, polled until the node was reachable again, confirmed the boot_id changed (proving an actual restart, not just a service bounce), and re-verified SELinux enforcing, httpd active/enabled and confined under httpd_t, port 8181 listening, firewall rule persisted, and the previously stored inventory item (\\\"Widget\\\", qty 42) still present.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS (AlmaLinux 9.6) and confirmed SELinux was already Enforcing (targeted policy)\",\"Installed httpd and policycoreutils-python-utils via dnf\",\"Created a Python CGI inventory application (/var/www/inventory-cgi/inventory.py) backed by SQLite (/var/www/inventory-data/inventory.db) supporting listing and adding items\",\"Configured /etc/httpd/conf.d/inventory.conf to Listen on 8181 and serve the CGI app as DocumentRoot via ScriptAlias\",\"Fixed a DAC ownership issue (chown apache:apache, chmod 770) on the data directory that was causing sqlite3.OperationalError\",\"Ran semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181 to authorize the confined httpd_t domain to bind port 8181 under SELinux\",\"Ran semanage fcontext to label the CGI script httpd_sys_script_exec_t and the data dir httpd_sys_rw_content_t, then restorecon -Rv\",\"Enabled and started httpd; verified it runs as system_u:system_r:httpd_t:s0 and listens on 0.0.0.0:8181 while SELinux remained Enforcing\",\"Opened firewalld port 8181/tcp permanently and reloaded\",\"Verified functional inventory app via curl GET and POST (added item Widget qty 42) from $NODE_IP\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime, SELinux mode, httpd status, listening port, semanage port mapping, and app data\",\"Issued a backgrounded systemctl reboot on node1 so the exec ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed boot_id changed and uptime reset, proving an actual OS restart\",\"Re-verified post-restart: SELinux still Enforcing, httpd active/enabled and running confined under httpd_t, port 8181 listening, firewall port persisted, semanage port mapping persisted, and the previously added inventory item persisted in the SQLite data\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"MAC (SELinux) is enforcing on node1 both before and after deployment\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b26b11bf2e234b4b\",\"cmd-1ed67a6268ca482b\",\"cmd-993f9bc5c15b48b4\",\"cmd-2203aa4e1a46439c\"],\"summary\":\"getenforce/sestatus show Enforcing at session start and immediately before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Inventory application is served over TCP port 8181 and functions (list + add items)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1c65f8d54dd64c1e\",\"cmd-9eb99949f14841b9\",\"cmd-2203aa4e1a46439c\"],\"summary\":\"After fixing directory ownership, GET returns 200 with rendered table; POST with name=Widget&quantity=42 successfully inserts and displays the new row; ss shows httpd LISTEN on *:8181\"},{\"requirement\":\"SELinux policy correctly configured (not bypassed) to allow the confined httpd_t domain to serve on 8181\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-21d939ed63e84f6b\",\"cmd-e2f7f42cc5524724\",\"cmd-116295ed0e814ea8\"],\"summary\":\"semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181 adds the port type; httpd starts successfully and ps -Z shows httpd processes labeled system_u:system_r:httpd_t:s0 while bound to 8181, with SELinux still Enforcing\"},{\"requirement\":\"External reachability opened via firewalld (not just loopback)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0f94ffb80d99474d\"],\"summary\":\"firewall-cmd --add-port=8181/tcp made permanent and reloaded; firewall-cmd --list-ports confirms 8181/tcp open\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline captured for node1 (boot identity + service/data health)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2203aa4e1a46439c\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id f43afa1c-4877-4ace-a101-d6bb0cd6ce3d, uptime since 22:53:19, SELinux Enforcing, httpd active/enabled, port 8181 listening, semanage mapping, and existing inventory row (Widget, 42) all before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-124282d6317442ac\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sleep 2 && systemctl reboot' returned 'reboot scheduled, pid 9627' immediately, before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart proven via changed boot identity (not just elapsed time or service restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bf1b16b747bf4541\",\"cmd-5254ccd2b5b6455e\",\"cmd-1a1e7abf70964046\"],\"summary\":\"First poll succeeded trivially (pre-drop), second poll hit connection timed out proving the node actually went down, third poll succeeded with new boot_id 18c8b181-09f3-42a8-a4c1-b4b1a94b7a14 (different from baseline) and fresh uptime since 22:55:22\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of MAC enforcement, service, port, firewall, and application data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fd3668aac63e4688\"],\"summary\":\"After restart: getenforce=Enforcing, httpd active/enabled and confined under httpd_t, ss shows LISTEN on 8181 with new httpd PIDs, firewalld still has 8181/tcp open, semanage port mapping intact, and curl GET shows the Widget/42 row persisted from before the reboot\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Built and deployed a small SQLite-backed CGI \"inventory application\" (add/list items) served by httpd on node1's TCP port 8181, with SELinux/mandatory access control kept in enforcing mode throughout. Configured semanage port to label 8181 as http_port_t (so the confined httpd_t domain is permitted to bind it), set correct file contexts (httpd_sys_script_exec_t for the CGI script, httpd_sys_rw_content_t for the writable data directory), opened the port in firewalld, verified end-to-end functionality (GET renders inventory table, POST adds an item and persists it), then executed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id and healthy baseline, issued systemctl reboot with the ack returned before disconnect, polled until the node was reachable again, confirmed the boot_id changed (proving an actual restart, not just a service bounce), and re-verified SELinux enforcing, httpd active/enabled and confined under httpd_t, port 8181 listening, firewall rule persisted, and the previously stored inventory item (\"Widget\", qty 42) still present.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS (AlmaLinux 9.6) and confirmed SELinux was already Enforcing (targeted policy)","Installed httpd and policycoreutils-python-utils via dnf","Created a Python CGI inventory application (/var/www/inventory-cgi/inventory.py) backed by SQLite (/var/www/inventory-data/inventory.db) supporting listing and adding items","Configured /etc/httpd/conf.d/inventory.conf to Listen on 8181 and serve the CGI app as DocumentRoot via ScriptAlias","Fixed a DAC ownership issue (chown apache:apache, chmod 770) on the data directory that was causing sqlite3.OperationalError","Ran semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181 to authorize the confined httpd_t domain to bind port 8181 under SELinux","Ran semanage fcontext to label the CGI script httpd_sys_script_exec_t and the data dir httpd_sys_rw_content_t, then restorecon -Rv","Enabled and started httpd; verified it runs as system_u:system_r:httpd_t:s0 and listens on 0.0.0.0:8181 while SELinux remained Enforcing","Opened firewalld port 8181/tcp permanently and reloaded","Verified functional inventory app via curl GET and POST (added item Widget qty 42) from $NODE_IP","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime, SELinux mode, httpd status, listening port, semanage port mapping, and app data","Issued a backgrounded systemctl reboot on node1 so the exec ack returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed boot_id changed and uptime reset, proving an actual OS restart","Re-verified post-restart: SELinux still Enforcing, httpd active/enabled and running confined under httpd_t, port 8181 listening, firewall port persisted, semanage port mapping persisted, and the previously added inventory item persisted in the SQLite data"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"MAC (SELinux) is enforcing on node1 both before and after deployment","command_ids":["cmd-b26b11bf2e234b4b","cmd-1ed67a6268ca482b","cmd-993f9bc5c15b48b4","cmd-2203aa4e1a46439c"],"summary":"getenforce/sestatus show Enforcing at session start and immediately before restart"},{"requirement":"Inventory application is served over TCP port 8181 and functions (list + add items)","command_ids":["cmd-1c65f8d54dd64c1e","cmd-9eb99949f14841b9","cmd-2203aa4e1a46439c"],"summary":"After fixing directory ownership, GET returns 200 with rendered table; POST with name=Widget&quantity=42 successfully inserts and displays the new row; ss shows httpd LISTEN on *:8181"},{"requirement":"SELinux policy correctly configured (not bypassed) to allow the confined httpd_t domain to serve on 8181","command_ids":["cmd-21d939ed63e84f6b","cmd-e2f7f42cc5524724","cmd-116295ed0e814ea8"],"summary":"semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181 adds the port type; httpd starts successfully and ps -Z shows httpd processes labeled system_u:system_r:httpd_t:s0 while bound to 8181, with SELinux still Enforcing"},{"requirement":"External reachability opened via firewalld (not just loopback)","command_ids":["cmd-0f94ffb80d99474d"],"summary":"firewall-cmd --add-port=8181/tcp made permanent and reloaded; firewall-cmd --list-ports confirms 8181/tcp open"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline captured for node1 (boot identity + service/data health)","command_ids":["cmd-2203aa4e1a46439c"],"summary":"Captured boot_id f43afa1c-4877-4ace-a101-d6bb0cd6ce3d, uptime since 22:53:19, SELinux Enforcing, httpd active/enabled, port 8181 listening, semanage mapping, and existing inventory row (Widget, 42) all before reboot"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection","command_ids":["cmd-124282d6317442ac"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'sleep 2 && systemctl reboot' returned 'reboot scheduled, pid 9627' immediately, before the node disconnected"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart proven via changed boot identity (not just elapsed time or service restart)","command_ids":["cmd-bf1b16b747bf4541","cmd-5254ccd2b5b6455e","cmd-1a1e7abf70964046"],"summary":"First poll succeeded trivially (pre-drop), second poll hit connection timed out proving the node actually went down, third poll succeeded with new boot_id 18c8b181-09f3-42a8-a4c1-b4b1a94b7a14 (different from baseline) and fresh uptime since 22:55:22"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of MAC enforcement, service, port, firewall, and application data","command_ids":["cmd-fd3668aac63e4688"],"summary":"After restart: getenforce=Enforcing, httpd active/enabled and confined under httpd_t, ss shows LISTEN on 8181 with new httpd PIDs, firewalld still has 8181/tcp open, semanage port mapping intact, and curl GET shows the Widget/42 row persisted from before the reboot"}]},"ttft_ms":2239,"type":"result","duration_ms":169823,"uuid":"4ce4cc71-8137-4d6e-b731-eebace3c8ebc","ttft_stream_ms":1558,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":2227,"queued_turn_count":0}
